      "topic_id": "frustum_volume_surface_area_H",
      "prompt": "A frustum is formed from a cone with a bottom radius of 14 cm and a top radius of 7 cm, and a vertical height of 14 cm. Find its volume, correct to 3 significant figures.",
      "solution_steps": [
        "Full cone height H = R × h ÷ (R - r) = 14 × 14 ÷ (14 - 7) = 28.00 cm (similar triangles)",
        "Big cone volume = (1/3) × π × R² × H, small cone volume = (1/3) × π × r² × (H - h)",
        "Frustum volume = (1/3) × π × h × (R² + Rr + r²) = (1/3) × π × 14 × (14² + 14×7 + 7²)",
        "= 5030 cm³ (3 s.f.)"
      ],
      "final_answer": "5030 cm³",
      "marks": 5,
